Yes, that’s right! Also, \(\sin140^\circ=\sin40^\circ\), \(\cos50^\circ=\sin40^\circ\), and \(\tan(-x)=-\tan x\). So:
\[
\frac{\sin140^\circ\cdot\sin(360^\circ-x)}{\cos50^\circ\cdot\tan(-x)}
=\frac{\sin40^\circ(-\sin x)}{\sin40^\circ(-\tan x)}
=\frac{\sin x}{\tan x}
=\frac{\sin x}{\sin x/\cos x}
=\boxed{\cos x}.
\]
No calculator needed—you got the key reduction!
